WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 8: Wonderful Water.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:10.580
In this unit you will learn about water — where it comes
from, where we find it, and all the ways we use it every day.

3
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.740
You will meet rainy and sunny
weather, animals that live in water,

4
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.600
and the big idea that water is a gift we should never waste.

5
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:26.820
Say the words out loud — this is about confident English
and being thankful for water, not perfect spelling.

6
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.960
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:39.280
By the end of this unit, you will be able to say
why plants, animals, and people all need water.

8
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:44.120
You will also name places where we
find water (rain, river, sea, well).

9
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.860
You will also say how we use water:
“I use water to drink / wash / cook.”

10
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

11
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:59.560
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: duck, sock, clock, queen, quick, quiz.

12
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:04.420
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

13
00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:10.000
The reading sequence includes The Well in
the Village and Talk about Wonderful Water.

14
00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.680
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

15
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:19.680
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

16
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.980
The first language focus is Say what you use water for.

17
00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.000
Think of one way you use water every day.

18
00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.840
After 'to', use the plain action word.

19
00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.740
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

20
00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:39.360
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

21
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.780
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

22
00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:49.140
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

23
00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.020
You are ready to begin.

24
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:57.180
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

25
00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:03.260
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
